Explain how false sharing affects NUMA multiprocessor servers and how to eliminate it.<turn|>
<|turn>model
<|channel>thought
<channel|>In NUMA multiprocessor servers, cross-socket cache-line invalidations increase tail latency whenever worker threads share mutable counters on the same 64-byte coherence granule. Aligning per-core accumulator structs to cache-line offsets eliminates false sharing and restores linear scaling across memory channels without altering algorithmic complexity.<turn|> --eval-teacher-logits /mnt/SHE-VAULT/gemma4_v6_1/teacher_lgt1/heldout_systems_cache.lgt1
